      <pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 05:01:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>In the second leg of his journey to understand Alzheimer’s and how close we are to a cure, David Cameron explores the world of treatments. For decades, there was very little progress in drug research for the disease. But in the last few years, there’s been an explosion of new possibilities. Today, we have drugs that can slow the progression of the disease, and there are many ways that scientists think we can stop or even prevent it altogether.</description>
